  <div class="wrap">
</div></div>

<div class="callout info" style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto 20px;text-align:center;">EFFECTIVE DATE NOTE: The revised Standard applied to insurers with both domestic and overseas listings from January 1, 2023 — aligned with IFRS 17's own international effective date — with other insurers following on a later timeline. This structural detail should be confirmed against current CAS materials given the complexity of insurer-specific transition arrangements.</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A comprehensive overhaul of insurance contract accounting</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 25 was COMPREHENSIVELY revised to INTRODUCE a MODERN measurement MODEL for DIRECT insurance CONTRACTS, CLOSELY mirroring IFRS 17'S own GENERAL measurement APPROACH internationally — a GENUINE landmark REFORM, replacing an OLDER, less CONSISTENT framework with a UNIFIED, principle-BASED model.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Direct Insurance, Not Reinsurance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Contracts issued directly to policyholders</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to DIRECT insurance CONTRACTS — those ISSUED directly by an INSURER to a POLICYHOLDER, ACCEPTING SIGNIFICANT insurance RISK from that POLICYHOLDER — WHEREAS reinsurance CONTRACTS (held or ISSUED) are GOVERNED separately by ASBE No. 26 (see the COMPANION poster).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The General Measurement Model — the Building Block Approach</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fulfilment cash flows plus a contractual service margin</div><div class="text-supporting">THE general MEASUREMENT model COMBINES (a) FULFILMENT cash FLOWS — a PROBABILITY-weighted estimate of FUTURE cash FLOWS, discounted, PLUS a RISK adjustment for NON-financial risk — WITH (b) a CONTRACTUAL SERVICE MARGIN (CSM) representing the UNEARNED profit the INSURER expects to EARN as it PROVIDES insurance COVERAGE over TIME — CONSISTENT with IFRS 17'S own "BUILDING BLOCK" approach internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Fulfilment Cash Flows</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Probability-weighted, discounted, with a risk adjustment</div><div class="text-supporting">FULFILMENT cash FLOWS comprise an UNBIASED, PROBABILITY-weighted ESTIMATE of FUTURE cash INFLOWS and OUTFLOWS (PREMIUMS, claims, EXPENSES), DISCOUNTED to REFLECT the time VALUE of MONEY, PLUS a RISK adjustment REFLECTING the compensation the INSURER requires for BEARING the uncertainty INHERENT in NON-financial risk.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>The Contractual Service Margin (CSM)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Unearned profit, released as coverage is provided</div><div class="text-supporting">THE CSM represents the UNEARNED profit an INSURER expects to EARN as it PROVIDES insurance COVERAGE — RECOGNISED in PROFIT or loss OVER the COVERAGE period as SERVICE is PROVIDED, RATHER than at CONTRACT inception — ENSURING profit RECOGNITION is SPREAD to REFLECT the ONGOING delivery of INSURANCE service.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The Premium Allocation Approach — a Simplified Alternative</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A simplified model for short-duration contracts</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR contracts with a COVERAGE period of ONE year or LESS (or WHERE the SIMPLIFIED approach WOULD produce a SIMILAR result to the GENERAL model), insurers MAY apply the PREMIUM ALLOCATION APPROACH (PAA) — a SIMPLIFIED model BROADLY resembling an "UNEARNED premium" APPROACH, AVOIDING the FULL complexity of the general BUILDING block MODEL for SHORT-duration business.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>A Structural Divergence — Two Separate Standards, Not One</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">China splits direct and reinsurance contracts into separate standards</div><div class="text-supporting">A GENUINELY notable STRUCTURAL feature: WHERE IFRS 17 is a SINGLE, unified STANDARD covering BOTH direct insurance CONTRACTS and reinsurance CONTRACTS TOGETHER, China SPLITS the EQUIVALENT guidance ACROSS TWO separate STANDARDS — THIS Standard for DIRECT contracts, and ASBE No. 26 for REINSURANCE contracts (see the COMPANION poster) — a STRUCTURAL, RATHER than substantive, DIVERGENCE, since the UNDERLYING measurement PRINCIPLES remain CLOSELY aligned across BOTH standards.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising the Contractual Service Margin</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Spreading unearned profit over the coverage period</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A 5-year life insurance contract group</div><div class="wk-body">An insurer issues a group of contracts with an initial CSM of RMB 50,000,000, expected to be released evenly over a 5-year coverage period.</div><div class="wk-answer">The insurer recognises CSM release (profit) of RMB 50,000,000 ÷ 5 = <strong>RMB 10,000,000 per year</strong>, RATHER than recognising the FULL expected PROFIT at CONTRACT inception.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Applying the Premium Allocation Approach</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A simplified model for a short-duration policy</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A 1-year property insurance policy</div><div class="wk-body">An insurer issues a 1-year property insurance policy for a premium of RMB 2,000,000, qualifying for the premium allocation approach.</div><div class="wk-answer">The insurer recognises REVENUE of RMB 2,000,000 ÷ 12 = <strong>RMB 166,667 per month</strong> over the COVERAGE period, a SIMPLIFIED, unearned-premium-STYLE approach AVOIDING the full BUILDING block model'S complexity.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 25 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Reconciliation of the insurance contract liability, including the CSM, from opening to closing balance</span><span>Significant judgements applied in applying the general model or the premium allocation approach</span><span>Nature and extent of risks arising from insurance contracts</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a contract qualifies for the premium allocation approach</span><span>Grouping of insurance contracts for measurement purposes</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Probability-weighted future cash flow estimates</span><span>Discount rates and the risk adjustment for non-financial risk</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 17</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 25 vs IFRS 17</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 25</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 17</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>General measurement model</span><span>Building block, with CSM</span><span>Building block, with CSM — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Standard structure</span><span>Separate standards for direct and reinsurance</span><span>ONE unified standard covering both</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED measurement MODEL, with a NOTABLE STRUCTURAL (not substantive) divergence in HOW the guidance is ORGANISED across STANDARDS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every insurance contract event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>CSM release</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised as insurance revenue over the coverage period</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 26</span><span>Reinsurance Contracts — the companion standard applying the same measurement principles to reinsurance-specific arrangements</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Contractual service margin (CSM)</div><div class="glossary-def">The unearned profit an insurer expects to earn from providing insurance coverage, recognised in profit or loss over the coverage period.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Premium allocation approach (PAA)</div><div class="glossary-def">A simplified measurement model available for short-duration insurance contracts, broadly resembling an unearned premium approach.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe25 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
